A comment with no terminating semicolon runs to the end of the file and
swallows everything after it (comment_termination). Formatting must leave
the swallowed text alone.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Demo;
:DECLARE nTotal;
nTotal := 1;
:ENDPROC;
/* trailing note that never ends
nTotal := 2
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Demo;
	:DECLARE nTotal;
	nTotal := 1;
:ENDPROC;
/* trailing note that never ends
nTotal := 2
-- diagnostics --
5:1-5:46 error comment_termination: SSL comments must end with a semicolon ';'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
5:1-5:46 error comment_termination: SSL comments must end with a semicolon ';'
